{
  "id": "early-bilingualism",
  "term": "early bilingualism",
  "definition": "Early bilingualism is growing up with two languages from infancy. In the source material, it is linked to a later decline in infants’ broad language-discrimination abilities, so bilingual infants can continue distinguishing between languages or signs at ages when monolingual infants often no longer do.",
